+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 */
+/*
+ * Kernel port of intfp - Integer-based Fixed-Point and Pseudo-Logarithmic
+ * Number Library, version 1.5.
+ *
+ * Upstream: https://github.com/firelzrd/intfp
+ *
+ * Porting notes (the numerics are kept byte-for-byte identical to upstream
+ * 1.5, only the two following mechanical changes were made):
+ *
+ *   1. <linux/types.h> is included, so u8/u16/u32/u64, s8/s16/s32/s64 and
+ *      bool come from the kernel instead of a freestanding toolchain.
+ *
+ *   2. Every function is turned into 'static inline' and every lookup table
+ *      into 'static const'.  Upstream ships them as externally linked
+ *      definitions, which would cause multiple-definition errors as soon as
+ *      the header is included by more than one translation unit, and would
+ *      pollute kallsyms/KMI with intfp symbols.  Being static inline /
+ *      static const, nothing is exported, no ABI/KMI surface is touched and
+ *      unused code is simply discarded by the compiler.
+ *
+ * Usage: #include <linux/intfp.h> and call the generated entry points, e.g.
+ *        u64_to_log32fpmax(), log32fpmax_to_u64(), u64_to_pul16fpmax(),
+ *        ewma_s32fp_div(), rescale_log32fp_to_radix().
+ */
+
